\"Initial empirical reference: DIN local activation over item-field history with action values and four separate heads; field/task adaptation, not exact original DIN reproduction\", \"research_goal\": \"Explore and validate mechanism-distinct unified modeling of multi-field user/context/target features and multi-feedback behavior histories. Develop representations and information flow that jointly support sequence modeling, feature interaction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\", \"architecture_search\": {\"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\", \"design_dimensions\": [\"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\", \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\", \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\", \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\", \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"], \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\", \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\", \"evidence\": \"Evaluate predictive quality, mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost. Compare new unified candidates against their closest architectural alternatives as well as the initial reference.\", \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\", \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspectable design references and nearest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"}, \"research_budget\": {\"seconds\": 172800, \"start_event\": \"dataset_download_and_checksum_verification_completed\", \"start_unix\": 1793959348.3455288, \"deadline_unix\": 1794132148.3455288}, \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\", \"source_sha256\": {\"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\", \"train.py\": \"e81bdefa140a4d78cae12f4123cc421611109c84da1b9f067e23d11b6c3d335a\", \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\", \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\"}, \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\", \"benchmark_deviations\": [\"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\", \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\", \"Click AUC selects models, four-task mean AUC is auxiliary.\", \"Validation includes every sample; upstream default drop_last may omit remainders.\", \"In-process DataLoader (num_workers=0): container shared memory is512MiB; all compared runs use the same loading policy.\", \"No torch.compile; BF16; TF32 disabled.\"], \"trial_cap_seconds\": 1203.3689693547785, \"estimated_unit_seconds\": 481.3475877419114, \"estimated_validation_seconds\": 75.22459795698524, \"frozen_unix\": 1793961097.640512, \"identity\": \"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\"}\nmethod \"auto\"\nbudget_scope \"The research wall clock starts at the recorded dataset download/checksum completion. Earlier acquisition and setup costs are reported separately; every later preparation step, calibration, agent call, failure, training/control and scoring job counts.\"\nno_test_feedback true\nknowledge_revision \"knowledge-access-v3\"\nknowledge_review {\"policy\": \"Evaluate relevant external references against local evidence; adoption is optional. Missing source detail and negative transfer remain explicit.\", \"proposal_output\": \"Add top-level knowledge_assessments: [{knowledge_id, decision: used|considered|rejected|unresolved, rationale, transformed_mechanism, variant_names, nearest_work_difference, falsifier}]. Cover retrieved industry cards; identify the concrete changed mechanism for used cards. This is provenance, not causal proof.\", \"reflection\": \"Review the latest knowledge-usage.json alongside outcomes; distinguish declared use, executed changes, mechanism evidence and unresolved attribution.\"}\nlatest_knowledge_usage {\"revision\": \"knowledge-access-v3\", \"retrieved_ids\": [\"unirank-method-hiformer\", \"unirank-method-infnet\", \"unirank-method-longer\", \"unirank-method-zenith\", \"unirank-method-hyformer\", \"unirank-method-hemix\", \"unirank-method-unimixer\", \"unirank-method-ultrahstu\", \"unirank-method-ssr\"], \"assessments\": [{\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-infnet\", \"decision\": \"used\", \"rationale\": \"The local auxiliary degradation makes historical feedback masks relevant; the pinned benchmark task-mask hub initialization was inspected. Original paper text remains unavailable.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"Use the already-authorized masks to partition compression groups, rather than initialize learned task hubs.\", \"variant_names\": [\"feedback_action\", \"rotated_action\", \"feedback_item\", \"rotated_item\"], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"No task tokens, hub projections or iterative aggregation/broadcast; inherited DIN readout.\", \"falsifier\": \"True grouping must improve on occupancy-matched rotation; otherwise this adaptation is unsupported.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:INFNet\", \"paper:infnet\"], \"executed_refs\": [{\"trial_id\": \"g2-r0001-feedback_action\", \"source_sha256\": \"fea5075bc5a2386f9f0aa825c66d7a0ef34bd570df64f73ce3a69c0d9bd28cd1\", \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"trial_id\": \"g2-r0001-rotated_action\", \"source_sha256\": \"e3b2d9471373ff5ee75977815a06e8b4790bf953f0f0fc8cab67632cd424bf83\", \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"trial_id\": \"g2-r0001-feedback_item\", \"source_sha256\": \"a36ca120262b4b79db493c5603c14302d74139cc213e1a221fcbcc2b3f1cd954\", \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"trial_id\": \"g2-r0001-rotated_item\", \"source_sha256\": \"25c59203389bde078a06822ae996bdf3182423bc981d31f3cc04070191673c81\", \"status\": \"success\"}], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-longer\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"Local group compression is inherited from the previous trajectory; pinned benchmark forward and section2.3 inspected. Original full paper is unavailable.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"No new LONGER component adopted; preserve arithmetic block summaries.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"Feedback membership and action-input factorial replace no inner Transformer or recent-query interaction.\", \"falsifier\": \"If measured cost is not below full-history DIN, the efficiency motivation fails for this implementation.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:LONGER\", \"paper:longer\"], \"executed_refs\": [], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-hiformer\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"Post-pooling field/task interaction is relevant but the observed task loss can first be tested with matched compression controls.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"Retain supplied task towers; no hierarchical field/task interaction blocks.\", \"falsifier\": \"This suite cannot establish a HiFormer effect; a separate matched architectural contrast is needed.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:HiFormer\", \"paper:hiformer\"], \"executed_refs\": [], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-hemix\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"Mixed fixed/feature-conditioned query banks are a possible future comparator, but the earlier target-category/brand branch did not improve click over simple pooling.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"No query bank or low-rank token mixer; explicit feedback grouping and inherited target activation.\", \"falsifier\": \"Null feedback grouping would leave the present hypothesis unsupported and would not refute HeMix.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:HeMix\", \"paper:hemix\"], \"executed_refs\": [], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-ssr\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"Post-pooling sparse filtering does not directly test loss of feedback association inside arithmetic means.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"No competitive sparse filtering or dense multi-view fusion.\", \"falsifier\": \"No local SSR claim is made or tested.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:SSR\", \"paper:ssr\"], \"executed_refs\": [], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-zenith\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"Changing identifier embedding capacity would add a distinct explanation to the compression contrast.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"All e